  "body": "Closes #9136 by adding a non-null browsing context check. Also updates to use \"in a document tree\" instead of \"in a document\".\n\nI'm omitting the PR checklist since this is basically a bug fix. Technically the clarification to use \"in a document tree\" could use some tests, but I'd rather not hold up the PR on that. I did make a  (Note that this is about old-and-ugly `frame`, not `iframe`.) Here's some confirmation though that `frame`s work inside shadow trees: https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=11512\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9139/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 10, 2023, 8:09 AM UTC (b0f5f55)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9139/1279623...b0f5f55/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 10, 2023, 8:09 AM UTC (b0f5f55)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9139/obsolete.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 10, 2023, 8:09 AM UTC (b0f5f55)\">/obsolete.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9139/1279623...b0f5f55/obsolete.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 10, 2023, 8:09 AM UTC (b0f5f55)\">diff</a> )",
